\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Place holder graphic. Caption to the effect of... The LO beam enters HAM6 directly above BHDBS2 (north side), and it is highlighted in green. A pick-off will be used to monitor the alignment of the LO; the pick-off beam is indicated with a dashed green line. The signal beam enters HAM6 directly above OM0 (north side), and it is highlighted in pink. The signal beam is steered by OM0 onto BHDBS2 where it is combined with the local oscillator. The shutter is located between OM0 and BHDBS2. A small amount of the signal beam is transmitted by OM0 (dashed pink); this beam is used align \ref  {}. The two combined beams are shown in red. These are incident upon a mirror used for steering (OMxS) and then upon two mirrors curved mirrors (OMx1 and OMx2). (Caption continued on next page).\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.8}}
